Tool.
  tool """" KeYmaera X """"
  model """" ArchiveEntry "SMIB asymptotic stability FULLY PARAMETRIC large-signal (D,K>0)"

/*
 * Single machine, ANY D>0, K>0 (no fixed values). Modified Hamiltonian
 *   V = H + a*w*sin(delta),  a = D*K/(K+D^2),
 * is a strict Lyapunov function on {cos(delta) >= 0}, establishing
 * asymptotic stability of the equilibrium -- LARGE-SIGNAL (full nonlinear
 * pendulum, no linearization), FULLY PARAMETRIC in D,K.
 *
 * V' = (a*c-2D)w^2 - a*D*w*s - a*K*s^2  (exact, nonlinear).
 * As a quadratic form in (w,s) it is negative definite on {c in [0,1]} iff
 *   (i)  a*c-2D < 0   and   (ii) det = a*K*(2D-a*c) - a^2 D^2/4 > 0.
 * With a=DK/(K+D^2):
 *   (i)  reduces to K*c < 2K+2D^2, true for all c<=1.
 *   (ii) det*(K+D^2)^2/(D^2 K^2) = 7D^2/4 - K*c + 2K = 7D^2/4 + K(2-c) > 0,
 *        true for all c<=2 (in particular c in [0,1]).
 * V>0: quadratic part [[1,a/2],[a/2,K]] has det K-a^2/4>0 since
 *   a=DK/(K+D^2) < 2*sqrt(K) (AM-GM: 2(K+D^2) > 4D*sqrt(K) > DK/...).
 *
 * Theorem (parametric QE): for all D,K>0 and all c in [0,1], the two
 * negative-definiteness conditions (i),(ii) and V>0 hold. Hence the exact
 * nonlinear single machine with any positive damping is asymptotically
 * stable with this explicit closed-form Lyapunov function.
 */

ProgramVariables Real D; Real K; Real c; End.

Problem
  \forall D \forall K \forall c (
    ( D > 0 & K > 0 & c >= 0 & c <= 1 )
    ->
    (   /* (i) w^2-coefficient negative: a*c-2D<0, cleared by (K+D^2)>0 */
        D*K*c - 2*D*(K+D^2) < 0
      & /* (ii) det>0, cleared form: 7D^2/4 + K*(2-c) > 0 */
        7*D^2/4 + K*(2-c) > 0
      & /* V>0: K - a^2/4 > 0, cleared by (K+D^2)^2>0 */
        K*(K+D^2)^2 - D^2*K^2/4 > 0 ) )
End.

Tactic "Proof" QE End.
End. """"
  tactic """" QE """"
  proof """"  """"
End.
